From c0c03bb41a7b86dd300774a0d583739a0353efdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:22:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: TEMPORARY -- bisect the render/flip stall three ways

Refines patch 0031's diagnostic. Removal is planned alongside it.

0031 established by direct measurement that the ~280ms mid-run stalls sit
entirely inside the render/flip span: pump_ms was 0.045ms and tail_ms
4.2ms on the stall frames, indistinguishable from every normal frame. So
audio and game logic are excluded, and the cost is somewhere in the span
that draws the world, scales it up, and pushes it to VRAM.

This splits that span: worldrender_ms (the game composing its own
buffer), blowup_ms (scaling into the window surface) and present_ms (the
VRAM flush).

Two things were ruled out by inspection rather than measurement first,
recorded so nobody re-treads them:

- The Cirrus LFB/VRAM-aperture defect (HARDWARE.md's known-issues table)
  is NOT live here. SDL/0019 and SDL/0020 are both applied, and the
  runtime log confirms 0019 acting: "LFB-decision #1: ...
  lfb_available=1 -> use_lfb=0", banked=1. The chip's defect is handled.

- blowUpChanged forcing a full-surface present is NOT the cause, despite
  looking conclusive in the source. That flag is set in exactly two
  places: its initial value, and inside a getKeyDown(SDL_SCANCODE_B)
  debug-key handler. During a normal run it fires once, on frame 1. A fix
  targeting it was written, verified visually, then reverted when the
  trigger was checked -- the mechanism was real but never fires.

Costs a normal frame a few clock reads and no file I/O; the emit is still
gated on an anomalous frame. Detector re-verified to fire before use, as
with 0031: thresholds lowered, all three new fields confirmed populating,
thresholds restored, rebuilt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index 652dd84..d276b3e 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -87,6 +87,15 @@ int blowUpStep = -1;
 // flag to force update of entire screen
 int blowUpChanged = true;
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+// TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC: sub-stage timings for the stall bisection, set
+// inside flipGameImageOntoScreen's native path and read by the STALLDBG
+// emit at the end of the loop. Globals rather than plumbing, because this
+// is temporary and plumbing would touch signatures that patch 0030 owns.
+Uint64 g_stallBlowupNS = 0;
+Uint64 g_stallPresentNS = 0;
+#endif
+
 
 char fullScreen = true;
 
@@ -448,6 +457,10 @@ void flipGameImageOntoScreen( SDL_Surface *inScreen ) {
             SDL_FillSurfaceRect( inScreen, NULL, 0 );
             }
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        const Uint64 stallBlowupT0 = SDL_GetTicksNS();
+#endif
+
         blowupOntoScreenNative( gameImage,
                                 width, totalImageHeight, blowUpFactor,
                                 inScreen );
@@ -456,6 +469,11 @@ void flipGameImageOntoScreen( SDL_Surface *inScreen ) {
             SDL_UnlockSurface( inScreen );
             }
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        const Uint64 stallBlowupT1 = SDL_GetTicksNS();
+        g_stallBlowupNS = stallBlowupT1 - stallBlowupT0;
+#endif
+
         SDL_Rect presentRect;
         presentRect.w = blowUpFactor * width;
         presentRect.h = blowUpFactor * totalImageHeight;
@@ -464,6 +482,10 @@ void flipGameImageOntoScreen( SDL_Surface *inScreen ) {
 
         presentScreen( inScreen, &presentRect, blowUpChanged );
 
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        g_stallPresentNS = SDL_GetTicksNS() - stallBlowupT1;
+#endif
+
         // we've handled any blow up change
         blowUpChanged = false;
         return;
@@ -1413,6 +1435,10 @@ char playGame() {
             }
             
         
+#ifdef __DJGPP__
+        const Uint64 stallTr = SDL_GetTicksNS();   // world render done
+#endif
+
         flipGameImageOntoScreen( screen );
 
 #ifdef __DJGPP__
@@ -2145,11 +2171,15 @@ char playGame() {
                 if( sf != NULL ) {
                     fprintf( sf,
                              "[stall] frame=%d work_ms=%f render_flip_ms=%f "
-                             "pump_ms=%f tail_ms=%f\n",
+                             "pump_ms=%f tail_ms=%f | worldrender_ms=%f "
+                             "blowup_ms=%f present_ms=%f\n",
                              frameCount, workMs,
                              (double)( stallT1 - stallT0 ) / 1000000.0,
                              (double)( stallT2 - stallT1 ) / 1000000.0,
-                             tailMs );
+                             tailMs,
+                             (double)( stallTr - stallT0 ) / 1000000.0,
+                             (double)g_stallBlowupNS / 1000000.0,
+                             (double)g_stallPresentNS / 1000000.0 );
                     fclose( sf );
                     }
                 }
